    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0985" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/6–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 568<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-23T20:00:00+02:00">June 23, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>197. Referring to Tito’s published remark
                    that problem of civil govt of Venezia Giulia is still open (Embtel 109 [<hi rendition="#italic">188</hi>],
                    June 22<anchor n="1" xml:id="d568-f1"/>) I suggest that US and UK govts instruct Belgrade Embassies to remind Yugo
                    Govt that question was settled by Article 3 of Belgrade Agreements and that
                    attempts to stir up trouble in area under AMG is
                    unlikely to benefit Yugos position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
